drm/omap: dss: don't warn about fck rounding differences

dss_set_fck_rate() warned when the clock framework's rate differed at all
from the requested one. The request comes from integer division of the
parent rate, so a few Hz of rounding is normal: on OMAP2420 (N800/N810)
every boot warned "clk rate mismatch: 131657142 != 131657144". Warn only
about differences above 10 ppm.

diff -uN a/drivers/gpu/drm/omapdrm/dss/dss.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/omapdrm/dss/dss.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/omapdrm/dss/dss.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/omapdrm/dss/dss.c
@@ -652,8 +652,14 @@
 
 	dss->dss_clk_rate = clk_get_rate(dss->dss_clk);
 
-	WARN_ONCE(dss->dss_clk_rate != rate, "clk rate mismatch: %lu != %lu",
-		  dss->dss_clk_rate, rate);
+	/*
+	 * The requested rate comes from integer division of the parent rate
+	 * and may differ from what the clock framework rounds to by a few Hz
+	 * (e.g. 131657142 vs 131657144 on OMAP2420); only warn about a real
+	 * mismatch.
+	 */
+	WARN_ONCE(abs_diff(dss->dss_clk_rate, rate) > rate / 100000,
+		  "clk rate mismatch: %lu != %lu", dss->dss_clk_rate, rate);
 
 	return 0;
 }
